  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAVING VALLES CENTRALES: SECURING GRASSLANDS CONNECTIVITY</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partners will expand their successful model of sustainable cattle ranching to include new ranches and properties within Valles Centrals, and to begin securing a biological corridor for focal migratory bird species within privately owned reserves. Pronatura Noreste has identified a set of properties in areas where the wintering population densities of focal grassland birds are highest. A total of 12,000 ha will be integrated into sustainable BMPs, through the creation of three private conservation reserves- El Roble, El15, and Las Damas. We will develop and implement sustainable livestock management plans for each of these reserves and, using bulldozers, restore 2940 ha of degraded grasslands. We also will continue to monitor densities of Neotropical birds within these reserves in order to measure the response of particular bird species to best management practices and restoration projects. Finally, we will continue building capacities, awareness, and interest in grassland birds among the ranchers by conducting an international workshop of experiences exchange.</narrative>
  </description>
